4,3.8,3.5,3.2,2.9,2.6,2.2],"g1":5.4,"g2":3.5,"g":2.25,"wacc":5.92,"ev":7744.8,"fmp_official_ev":7744.8,"enterpriseValueBasis":"USD market capitalization + USD debt - USD cash and short-term investments","dcf_model_ev":7174.5,"ev_to_ebitda":13.4,"debt_to_ebitda":4.35,"net_debt_to_ebitda":4.33,"f_score":5,"f_score_breakdown":[{"id":1,"category":"盈利能力","desc":"資產回報率 ROA > 0","passed":1,"detail":"當期 ROA = 3.3%"},{"id":2,"category":"盈利能力","desc":"營業現金流 CFO > 0","passed":1,"detail":"自由現金流 = $227M"},{"id":3,"category":"盈利能力","desc":"資產回報率持續擴張 (ΔROA > 0)","passed":0,"detail":"回報率穩步領先同業基準"},{"id":4,"category":"盈利能力","desc":"應計利潤品質高 (CFO > 淨利潤)","passed":1,"detail":"真實現金流充沛，無虛報帳面獲利"},{"id":5,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"財務槓桿未惡化 (ΔLeverage ≤ 0)","passed":1,"detail":"總負債資產比率 = 51.4%"},{"id":6,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"短期流動性安全 (ΔLiquidity > 0)","passed":0,"detail":"流動比率 = 0.51"},{"id":7,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"股本未遭稀釋 (ΔShares ≤ 0)","passed":1,"detail":"未大幅增發新股割韭菜"},{"id":8,"category":"營運效率","desc":"毛利率擴張 (ΔMargin > 0)","passed":0,"detail":"產品定價權增強，毛利結構健康"},{"id":9,"category":"營運效率","desc":"資產週轉率提升 (ΔTurnover > 0)","passed":0,"detail":"每單位資產產出效益改善"}],"fair_val":36.14,"default_fair_val":36.14,"premium_pct":12.2,"is_undervalued":false,"pe_trailing":28.8,"pe_forward":25.3,"pb_trailing":2.2,"pb_forward":2,"div_yield":3.18,"ps_ratio":5.8,"fcf_to_ev":2.93,"fcf_to_mcap":4.33,"liab_to_assets":51.4,"cash_to_assets":0.2,"current_ratio":0.51,"roe":7.5,"roa":3.3,"moat":{"ticker":"PECO","period":"2026Q3","m1_brand_pricing":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"Phillips Edison & Co. 在零售房地產 REIT 領域，透過其自有品牌超市（如 Publix、Kroger 等）的穩定租賃組合，展現了一定的品牌定價能力。其租戶組合的多元化和對必需消費品的依賴，使其在經濟波動中具有相對穩定的租金收入。然而，與消費品品牌相比，其品牌影響力在租戶選擇上並非絕對主導，租戶仍有其他選擇。因此，其品牌定價權屬於中等水平，能夠在一定程度上轉嫁成本，但並非無可匹敵的壁壘。","comment_en":"Phillips Edison & Co. demonstrates moderate brand pricing power within the retail real estate REIT sector, leveraging its portfolio of grocery-anchored centers (e.g., with tenants like Publix, Kroger). The diversification of its tenant base and reliance on essential consumer goods contribute to relatively stable rental income during economic fluctuations. However, compared to consumer product brands, its brand influence is not absolute in tenant selection, as tenants still have alternative locations. Therefore, its brand pricing power is considered moderate, allowing for some cost pass-through, but it does not represent an insurmountable barrier."},"m2_patents_regulatory":{"score":1,"comment_zh":"作為一家零售房地產投資信託公司，Phillips Edison & Co. 的業務模式不依賴於專利或特許經營權。其核心競爭力在於地產的選址、開發、運營和租賃管理。這類業務的進入壁壘主要來自於資本、經驗和網絡，而非受專利保護的技術或獨家許可。因此，在專利和監管壁壘方面，該公司幾乎沒有護城河可言，得分極低。","comment_en":"As a retail real estate investment trust, Phillips Edison & Co.'s business model does not rely on patents or exclusive licenses. Its core competencies lie in property selection, development, operation, and lease management. The barriers to entry in this type of business are primarily capital, experience, and networks, rather than patented technology or exclusive permits. Consequently, the company possesses virtually no moat in terms of patents and regulatory barriers, scoring extremely low."},"m3_high_switching_costs":{"score":5,"comment_zh":"對於 Phillips Edison & Co. 的租戶而言，轉換成本相對較高。一旦租戶在某個地理位置建立了業務，並依賴該地點的客流量和社區關係，搬遷至新的地點將涉及顯著的成本，包括裝修、重新建立客戶群、以及潛在的租金差異。特別是對於依賴特定地理位置的零售商，這種轉換成本會更加明顯。然而，若市場上有更具吸引力的替代地點，租戶仍有可能選擇轉換，因此轉換成本的壁壘並非絕對。","comment_en":"For Phillips Edison & Co.'s tenants, switching costs are relatively significant. Once a tenant establishes a business at a particular location and relies on its foot traffic and community relationships, relocating to a new site incurs substantial costs, including renovations, rebuilding customer bases, and potential rent differentials. This is particularly true for retailers dependent on specific geographic locations. However, if more attractive alternative locations become available in the market, tenants may still opt to switch, meaning the switching cost barrier is not absolute."},"m4_network_effects":{"score":2,"comment_zh":"Phillips Edison & Co. 的業務模式並未體現顯著的網絡效應。雖然一個成功的購物中心可能吸引更多租戶和消費者，形成一定的聚集效應，但這更多是基於地理位置和業態組合的吸引力，而非傳統意義上的網絡效應，即用戶越多，服務價值越高的情況。其租戶之間的協同效應有限，消費者對單一購物中心的忠誠度也相對較低，不具備強大的網絡效應壁壘。","comment_en":"Phillips Edison & Co.'s business model does not exhibit significant network effects. While a successful shopping center might attract more tenants and consumers, creating a clustering effect, this is more attributable to the attractiveness of the location and tenant mix rather than traditional network effects where the service value increases with more users. The synergy among its tenants is limited, and consumer loyalty to a single shopping center is relatively low, thus lacking a strong network effect barrier."},"m5_cost_advantage_scale":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"作為一家擁有大量零售物業組合的 REIT，Phillips Edison & Co. 透過規模化經營，在採購、融資、物業管理和營銷方面享有一定的成本優勢。大規模的採購能力有助於降低維護和營運成本，而較大的資產規模則能吸引更優惠的融資條件。這種規模經濟有助於其在行業內保持競爭力，並可能對小型競爭對手構成一定的進入壁壘，但相較於某些製造業或科技業的規模優勢，其成本節約的幅度相對有限。","comment_en":"As a REIT with a substantial portfolio of retail properties, Phillips Edison & Co. benefits from certain cost advantages in procurement, financing, property management, and marketing due to its scaled operations. Large-scale purchasing power helps reduce maintenance and operational costs, while a larger asset base can attract more favorable financing terms. This economy of scale aids in maintaining competitiveness within the industry and may pose a barrier to smaller competitors. However, the extent of cost savings is relatively limited compared to the scale advantages seen in some manufacturing or technology sectors."},"m6_unique_geography_assets":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"Phillips Edison & Co. 的資產組合主要集中在美國特定區域，尤其是在人口增長較快、經濟穩定的地區。這些地理位置的選擇，若能精準把握當地社區的發展趨勢和居民消費需求，便能形成一定的區域性優勢。然而，房地產的獨特性在於其地理位置，但優秀的地理位置並非絕對稀缺，競爭對手亦可能在同一區域開發或收購類似資產。因此，其獨特地理資產的壁壘屬於中等水平，依賴於持續的精準選址和開發能力。","comment_en":"Phillips Edison & Co.'s asset portfolio is primarily concentrated in specific regions of the United States, particularly in areas with faster population growth and stable economies. If these locations are chosen by accurately capturing local community development trends and resident consumption needs, they can form a certain regional advantage. However, while real estate is unique due to its location, prime locations are not absolutely scarce, and competitors may also develop or acquire similar assets in the same areas. Therefore, the barrier from its unique geographic assets is moderate, relying on continuous precise site selection and development capabilities."},"m7_operational_efficiency":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Phillips Edison & Co. 作為一家專業的零售房地產 REIT，其營運效率是其核心競爭力之一。公司在物業管理、租戶關係維護、租金徵收和資產優化方面擁有成熟的體系和經驗。透過精細化的營運管理，能夠最大化資產的租金收入和利用率，並有效控制營運成本。相較於非專業的物業持有者，其營運效率的領先優勢構成了一定的護城河，有助於在競爭激烈的市場中保持穩健的表現。","comment_en":"As a specialized retail real estate REIT, Phillips Edison & Co.'s operational efficiency is one of its core competencies. The company possesses a mature system and experience in property management, tenant relationship maintenance, rent collection, and asset optimization. Through refined operational management, it can maximize rental income and utilization rates of its assets while effectively controlling operating costs. Compared to non-professional property owners, its leading edge in operational efficiency constitutes a certain moat, contributing to a stable performance in a competitive market."},"m8_capital_allocation":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"Phillips Edison & Co. 的資本配置能力體現在其對物業組合的選擇、收購、開發和融資決策上。公司需要審慎評估市場機會，將資本投入到回報潛力高且風險可控的項目中。其作為 REIT 的結構，要求將大部分利潤以股息形式分配給股東，這限制了其留存收益再投資的能力。儘管如此，若公司能持續透過有效的融資和精準的投資，實現資產的增值和租金收入的增長，則其資本配置能力仍可視為中等水平的護城河。","comment_en":"Phillips Edison & Co.'s capital allocation capability is reflected in its decisions regarding property portfolio selection, acquisition, development, and financing. The company must prudently evaluate market opportunities and invest capital in projects with high return potential and controllable risks. Its structure as a REIT necessitates distributing most profits as dividends to shareholders, limiting its ability to reinvest retained earnings. Nevertheless, if the company can consistently achieve asset appreciation and rental income growth through effective financing and precise investments, its capital allocation capability can be considered a moderate moat."},"m9_customer_retention":{"score":5,"comment_zh":"Phillips Edison & Co. 的客戶（租戶）留存率受到其物業位置、租金水平、物業管理服務以及租戶自身業務發展等多重因素影響。公司透過提供良好的購物環境和穩定的租賃條款，努力維持租戶的忠誠度。然而，零售業的競爭激烈，租戶的經營狀況波動較大，這使得客戶留存並非易事。若其租戶主要是必需消費品零售商，則留存率可能相對較高，但整體而言，其客戶留存壁壘屬於中等。","comment_en":"Phillips Edison & Co.'s customer (tenant) retention rate is influenced by multiple factors, including property location, rental rates, property management services, and the tenant's own business development. The company strives to maintain tenant loyalty by providing a good shopping environment and stable lease terms. However, the retail industry is highly competitive, and tenant business conditions can fluctuate significantly, making customer retention challenging. If its tenants are primarily essential goods retailers, retention rates might be relatively higher, but overall, its customer retention barrier is moderate."},"m10_durability":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"Phillips Edison & Co. 的業務模式具有一定的持久性，主要得益於其對必需消費品零售商的依賴以及在特定社區建立的穩固地位。零售 REIT 的核心資產是房地產，其價值相對穩定，且能產生持續的現金流。然而，線上零售的興起對傳統零售業構成長期挑戰，這可能影響其部分租戶的經營狀況和對實體店面的需求。儘管如此，其專注於必需消費品和社區型購物中心的策略，使其在面對顛覆性創新時，仍具備一定的韌性和持久性。","comment_en":"Phillips Edison & Co.'s business model possesses a degree of durability, primarily due to its reliance on essential consumer goods retailers and its established position within specific communities. The core assets of a retail REIT are real estate, which holds relatively stable value and generates consistent cash flow. However, the rise of e-commerce poses a long-term challenge to traditional retail, potentially impacting the business conditions of some tenants and the demand for physical storefronts. Despite this, its strategy of focusing on essential goods and community-centric shopping centers provides it with a certain resilience and durability against disruptive innovations."},"overall_moat_verdict_zh":"Phillips Edison & Co. 作為一家零售房地產 REIT，其經濟護城河主要體現在規模帶來的成本優勢（M5）和穩健的營運效率（M7）上。其地理位置的選擇（M6）和租戶轉換成本（M3）也提供了一定的保護。然而，公司缺乏專利或網絡效應等強大壁壘（M2, M4），且品牌定價權（M1）和客戶留存（M9）相對有限。業務的持久性（M10）受到線上零售的潛在影響。整體而言，其護城河屬於中等水平，更像是一個穩健的『收費橋』模式，依賴於精選的優質地產組合和高效的營運管理，而非難以逾越的競爭壁壘。","overall_moat_verdict_en":"As a retail real estate REIT, Phillips Edison & Co.'s economic moat primarily lies in its cost advantages derived from scale (M5) and robust operational efficiency (M7). Its strategic location selection (M6) and tenant switching costs (M3) also offer some protection. However, the company lacks strong barriers such as patents or network effects (M2, M4), and its brand pricing power (M1) and customer retention (M9) are relatively limited. The durability of its business (M10) is subject to the potential impact of online retail. Overall, its moat is moderate, resembling a stable 'toll bridge' model that relies on a carefully selected portfolio of quality properties and efficient operational management, rather than insurmountable competitive barriers.","evidenceHash":"20fdc7d235e0dadc358791aaa3068069b43c32aaccda578652b4da34228539e9","assessmentPolicy":"buffett-moat-v3","model":"gemini-2.5-flash-lite","provider":"Vertex AI"},"ratingSources":{"moat":{"reason":null,"evidenceHash":"20fdc7d235e0dadc358791aaa3068069b43c32aaccda578652b4da34228539e9","currentEvidenceHash":"20fdc7d235e0dadc358791aaa3068069b43c32aaccda578652b4da34228539e9"},"fScore":{"score":5,"checkedAt":null},"zScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-12-31","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":"z","zone":"distress","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-11-08T12:12:55.939Z","evidenceHash":"7dfcfdc403ea0ce2a04be112f9d1139acd67355c1af3896bed87ff1cfe1ffc3f"},"mScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-12-31","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":null,"zone":"clean","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-11-08T12:12:55.939Z","evidenceHash":"7dfcfdc403ea0ce2a04be112f9d1139acd67355c1af3896bed87ff1cfe1ffc3f"}},"fin_valuation":{"is_financial":false},"image":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/PECO.png","logo":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/PECO.png","website":"https://www.phillipsedison.com","ceo":"Jeffrey S. Edison","full_time_employees":"320","description":"Phillips Edison & Company, Inc. is one of the nation’s largest owners and operators of high-quality, grocery-anchored neighborhood shopping centers. PECO has generated strong results through its vertically integrated operating platform and national footprint of well-occupied shopping centers. PECO’s centers feature a mix of national and regional retailers providing necessity-based goods and services in fundamentally strong markets throughout the United States. PECO’s top grocery anchors include Kroger, Publix, Albertsons and Ahold Delhaize. As of December 31, 2025, PECO managed 324 shopping centers, including 297 wholly owned centers comprising 33.5 million square feet across 31 states and 27 shopping centers owned in three institutional joint ventures. PECO is focused on creating great omni-channel, grocery-anchored shopping experiences and improving communities, one neighborhood shopping center at a time. Phillips Edison & Company, Inc. was incorporated in 1991.","description_en":"Phillips Edison & Company, Inc. is one of the nation’s largest owners and operators of high-quality, grocery-anchored neighborhood shopping centers. PECO has generated strong results through its vertically integrated operating platform and national footprint of well-occupied shopping centers. PECO’s centers feature a mix of national and regional retailers providing necessity-based goods and services in fundamentally strong markets throughout the United States. PECO’s top grocery anchors include Kroger, Publix, Albertsons and Ahold Delhaize. As of December 31, 2025, PECO managed 324 shopping centers, including 297 wholly owned centers comprising 33.5 million square feet across 31 states and 27 shopping centers owned in three institutional joint ventures. PECO is focused on creating great omni-channel, grocery-anchored shopping experiences and improving communities, one neighborhood shopping center at a time. Phillips Edison & Company, Inc. was incorporated in 1991.","description_zh":"Phillips Edison & Co.（美股代碼：PECO）為 Real Estate 領域之重要企業，專注於 REIT - Retail 業務，具備清晰之商業壁壘與現金流創造能力。","address":"11501 Northlake Drive","city":"Cincinnati","state":"OH","zip":"45249","country":"US","phone":"(513) 554-1110","full_address":"11501 Northlake Drive, Cincinnati, OH 45249, US","range_52w":"34.22-44.38","year_high":44.38,"year_low":34.22,"all_time_high":0,"all_time_low":34.22,"inst_ownership_pct":null,"insider_ownership_pct":null,"top_holders":[],"insider_trades":[{"date":"2026-05-14","name":"Fischer Elizabeth","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":2901,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-05-14","name":"QUAZZO STEPHEN R","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":2901,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-05-14","name":"Silfen Jane","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":2901,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-05-14","name":"Strong John A.","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":2901,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-05-14","name":"Wood Gregory S.","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":2901,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-05-14","name":"Terry Anthony E","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":2901,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-05-14","name":"CHAO LESLIE T","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":2901,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-05-14","name":"Murphy Devi